+---
+id: dl-002-availability-reuses-period-validation-and-overlap-rules-sorts-ids-ascending
+type: decision-log
+title: "availability() reuses period validation and overlap rules, sorts ids ascending"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The desk needs `availability(query)` on `createRentalService()` to see at a glance which equipment of a
+kind (or any kind) is free for a whole period. It had to fit the storage model and interval semantics
+already decided in dl-001.
+
+## Decision
+
+- **Period validation**: `availability` validates `start`/`end` with the existing `wholeDaysBetween`
+  helper, the same one `quote`/`book` use. An invalid period (not whole UTC days, or `end` not after
+  `start`) throws rather than returning an empty list, matching `quote`/`book`'s behaviour for the same
+  input errors.
+- **"Free for the whole period"**: an item is free when none of its existing bookings overlaps the query
+  period, reusing the half-open `overlaps` check from dl-001. A booking ending exactly when the query
+  starts (or starting exactly when it ends) does not block the item, consistent with back-to-back
+  bookings being allowed.
+- **`kind` filter**: when `kind` is given, only equipment of that kind is considered; when omitted, every
+  kind is considered. No validation is added for an invalid `kind` string beyond what TypeScript's type
+  already guarantees, since (unlike `addEquipment`) this is an internal desk query, not data that gets
+  stored.
+- **Result order**: ids are returned sorted with the default string sort (ascending), so the result is
+  deterministic regardless of `Map` insertion order, per the project's determinism directive.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Behaviour stays consistent with `quote`/`book`: the same period is valid or invalid everywhere in the
+  service.
+- Callers get a deterministic, directly displayable list without needing to sort client-side.
